# Files a kernel debugger sent with `remote put` (docs/kdebug-design.md),
# written to disk once the machine runs again. EXITS AT ONCE on a boot
# with no `kdebug=` -- the kernel says so -- and the default
# Restart=on-failure leaves a clean exit alone, so it costs nothing there.
Name=kdfiled
Description=Write files sent through the kernel debugger
Exec=/bin/kdfiled
